# @NAME@

A game on [Kerosene](https://github.com/t342guy/kerosene).

```sh
cargo play                 # build what changed, then play
cargo play +map @MAP@      # any console command after it
cargo tools chisel content/maps/@MAP@.keromap   # edit the map
cargo ship                 # build everything properly, into dist/
```

The first `cargo play` builds the engine and its tools, which takes a few
minutes. After that it rebuilds only what changed.

- `src/game.rs`: the game. One class of its own, `item_pickup`.
- `src/main.rs`: the binary. `@PACKAGE@ --headless 600` is a dedicated server.
- `src/tools.rs`: the editor and compilers, knowing this game's classes.
- `content/`: maps, textures, models, sounds, scripts and UI. Anything the
  engine's base content has (dev textures, the stock HUD) can be replaced by
  putting a file at the same path here.

On Linux, sound needs the ALSA headers (`libasound2-dev` or
`alsa-lib-devel`). Without them, build with `--no-default-features`.
